Main CI reports sooner. .github/workflows/gate.yml:
- runs spec check once per job;
- runs the tests in shards: 3 per Linux job and 2 per macOS job, for each Node version, which fits GitHub's limit of 5 concurrent macOS jobs on a public repository;
- keeps fail-fast off, so one shard's failure never hides another's;
- adds a concurrency group per ref, so a newer push to main cancels a run still in progress for an older one, and pull requests and manual runs are never cancelled;
- keeps the job names showing OS, Node version and shard, as linux (24) 1/3.
A test in test/workflows.test.js, "the gate workflow shards and cancels superseded main runs", reads the workflow. It checks that the shards of each OS and Node version cover 1 to n, that every job still runs spec check, that the concurrency group cancels only on main, and that fail-fast stays off. The gate passes.

